<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistani rice export prices seen falling.</title>
<headline>Pakistani rice export prices seen falling.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistani rice export prices are likely to fall in the next trading week starting on Saturday because of low demand from abroad and the arrival of the new crop, dealers said.</p>
<p>&quot;Rice prices are likely to fall in the next few days,&quot; one dealer said.</p>
<p>In the local market, prices of new crop rice were likely to remain mixed, he said.</p>
<p>The crops of both IRRI-6 and Basmati varieties were good with healthy grains.  </p>
<p>Following are exporters' FOB rates per tonne:</p>
<p>						 Thursday    Sept 19</p>
<p>    Basmati				  $433.75     $433.75</p>
<p>    IRRI-6				   not quoted  not quoted</p>
<p>Prices in the domestic markets in rupees per 100 kg:</p>
<p>						 Thursday    Sept 19</p>
<p>    Basmati (old)			  1,650/1,800 1,650/1,850</p>
<p>    Basmati (new)			  1,500/1,650 1,475/1,625</p>
<p>    IRRI-6				     800/825     800/825</p>
<p>($1 = 37.06 rupees)</p>
<p>--Ibrahim Khan 9221-5685192</p>
